# River boulders: rounded, water-worn boulders standing in a river's bed and on its banks - where the water runs FAST
# (rapids, a steep stream), almost none in slow water. A River rule: it may place inside the bed (Terrain/Rivers/
# Vegetation clear keeps every other rule out) and, with the negative Altitude, under the water. Format:
# Code/Procedural/CONTEXT.md, "Rocks".
RockType RiverBoulder
	Seed 31
	Scale 0.8 2.6
	Variants 6
	Sink 0.25
	Shape Boulder
	Aspect 1 0.65 0.8
	AspectVar 0.15 0.2 0.15
	Round 0.1
	Erosion 0.25
	Warp 0.04 1.2
	Fracture 2 0.15
	Noise 0.02 2.0 4
	Lod 1600
	Placement
		Density 120
		River 0 1
		Flow 0.03 1
		Altitude -4 100000
		Slope 0 0 0.6 1.2
		Cluster 25 0.6
